hrtf.sofa: derived from the TH Koeln Neumann KU100 HRIR measurements (Benjamin Bernschuetz,
https://zenodo.org/records/3928297), licensed CC BY-SA 3.0; this derived file is distributed under the same
license. Changes: subset of the 2-degree Gauss grid, minimum phase with a frequency-dependent interaural
delay, magnitudes matched to measurements of Apple's generic Spatial Audio rendering.

room.wav: synthesized by tools/build_binaural.py.

brir.wav: the HeSuVi forum community capture of Apple's generic Spatial Audio rendering (AppleSpatialAudio+, posted
by "3 DJ" in the "Apple Spatial Audio" thread), trimmed by a common lead-in and reordered per virtual speaker. The
capture carries no license, and the rendering it records is Apple's. It is included so fixed mode reproduces that
rendering exactly; confirm you may redistribute it before publishing a package (e.g. to the KDE Store). Without it,
build the other assets only (hrtf.sofa, room.wav) and fixed mode needs a different source.
